## 6. Debugging History & Failure Modes

- Chromium was absent on the first E2E run; installing the Playwright browser resolved it.
- A theme button changes accessible name with state, so tests must assert the current name.
- CSS display declarations can override the HTML `hidden` contract; preserve the global
  `[hidden]` rule.
- Skip links can appear in full-page captures if offscreen styling is incomplete.
- Filling a long textarea programmatically can leave the mobile view scrolled; reset selection and
  scroll position after loading a sample.
- Static secret scanners can match their own pattern declarations; keep scanners scoped.
- Shared developer machines can already use a conventional preview port. NoteDock uses `4175`
  after `4173` was confirmed to belong to an unrelated process; never kill an unverified listener.
- Export assertions must reflect the real Markdown contract, including bold timecode delimiters.
- Invalid framed timecodes must remain visible and untimed with a precise issue rather than being
  silently accepted.
- Clipboard APIs can be denied; preserve the CSV recovery path and user-visible status.
- CSV exports must neutralize formula-leading client text before spreadsheet use.

